\value{
\code{go_*()} functions return a graph object;
  \code{add_*()} functions return the modified figure.
}
\description{
In vertical (horizontal) violin plots, statistics are computed using `y`
(`x`) values. By supplying an `x` (`y`) array, one violin per distinct x
(y) value is drawn If no `x` (`y`) vector is provided, a single violin is
drawn. That violin position is then positioned with `name` or with `x0`
(`y0`) if provided.
}
